      "title": "V2 CORE / FL2VA WORKFLOW — HOW TO USE IT",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "This workflow intentionally has no reference scheduler and uses ComfyUI's core MiniMaxH3ImageToVideo node. With both image sockets connected it is FL2VA; disconnect Picture 2 for I2VA, disconnect Picture 1 for L2VA, or disconnect both for T2VA.\n\n1. Select real opening and ending images. The bundled filenames are placeholders.\n2. In Scene Prompt Editor, replace the generic motion path with what visibly connects those exact frames. Keep the first FL2VA alignment line and its 5.17-second endpoint because this plan uses exactly 124 raw frames.\n3. Click @ Reference to inspect Picture 1 and Picture 2; hover either chip for its image preview. These are native keyframe labels, not scheduled aliases.\n4. Queue, then use Review Gate to approve, edit+retry, reroll, or stop.\n5. Final Assemble preserves generated audio and uses a date token. Existing files receive _001, _002, and so on.\n\nThe one-scene plan is deliberate: a globally connected first/last pair would otherwise be reapplied to every recursive scene. For a long T2VA continuation, disconnect both keyframes and add scenes. For a later isolated FL2VA scene, use a one-scene plan or render it as its own run."
      ],
      "color": "#432f66",
      "bgcolor": "rgba(24,24,27,.9)"
    },
