      "title": "FL2VA PLAN QUICK REFERENCE",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "CORE FL2VA — QUICK FORMAT\n\nThis demo is one exact 124-frame (5.17 s) transition. Keep the first alignment line synchronized with the node length:\n\nHow the reference pictures align with the target video — Picture 1 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 0.00-second mark of the target video; Picture 2 (from Shot 1) aligns with the 5.17-second mark of the target video.\n\nThen write exactly these fields in order:\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Describe the continuous visible path from Picture 1 to Picture 2.\n\noverall_soundscape: Describe ambience and synchronized physical sounds.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Describe audience-only music, or N/A.\n\nBoth keyframes connected = FL2VA. Only first = I2VA. Only last = L2VA, where the lone last frame is called <Picture 1>. Neither = T2VA.\n\nUse one scene when a global first/last pair must apply once. For a long T2VA continuation, disconnect both images before adding scenes. Plan uses generated_audio, so no source-song wiring is required."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
